WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.640
These students at the University of Toronto

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.720
are angry

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.859
because a so-called

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.860
men's rights activist was speaking

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.540
at their college.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.500
His words are hate speech, they said.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.460
No hate speech on campus!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.760
They stopped people like this man

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.300
from getting in to see the lecture.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.760
The boy crisis.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.020
The so-called men's rights advocate

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.240
speaking inside was Warren Farrell.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.960
For the first time in US history,

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.820
boys will have less education than their dads.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.820
Farrell is an odd person to call anti-woman.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.480
He was actually an early feminist movement leader.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.640
Here he is with Gloria Steinem.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.380
But as he learned more,

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.320
he started to disagree with parts of modern feminism.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.860
I don't agree with the part of feminism

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.600
that says men are the oppressors

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.240
and women are the oppressed.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.160
That part of feminism is sick.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.680
Men are running the government,

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.100
they run most companies,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.540
they make more money.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:06.240
Our dads and our grandpas, they made sacrifices

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.620
to make more money and then the feminist movement

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.640
turned all of that sacrifice on the part of men

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.240
against men

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.780
and they haven't said you were discriminated against

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.240
men in your own way,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.220
you were obliged to earn more money

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.111
or we wouldn't even be thinking about marrying you.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:23.500
We wouldn't be thinking about having

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.760
children with you.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.940
In his book The Boy Crisis,

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.140
Farrell notes that both sexes struggle.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.540
Today, boys are almost 1/3 less likely

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.680
to get college degrees than girls,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.340
twice as likely to commit suicide.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.280
Why is no one talking about this?

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.280
Because we have believed for the last 50 years

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.540
that men had all the privilege and men had all the power.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.760
Men and boys started falling behind

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:47.960
when government began

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.100
subsidizing single mothers.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.540
They tear the family apart

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.820
by giving money to mothers

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.840
when fathers are absent

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.380
and not giving money to mothers

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.500
when fathers are present.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.460
That policy,

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.440
part of the welfare system created in the 60's

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.720
helped lead to more households without fathers.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.327
Farrell says that hurts boys most.

00:02:09.327 --> 00:02:12.060
Why are boys more affected than girls?

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.560
Boys tend to not have as many skills

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.320
at developing friendships

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.360
and developing emotional connections

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.080
and so when the family connection breaks apart,

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.650
it affects them more profoundly

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.040
than it does their sisters.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.520
This 1989 CBS interview

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.520
captured the changing attitudes

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.540
after welfare programs started.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.030
I think I can make it as a single parent.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.920
But don't you think you might need help

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.300
in raising that baby, from a man?

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.320
Not really.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.500
It doesn't make any difference

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:43.079
whether she needs a man, it makes a difference that

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.360
her children need a father.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.520
What happens when the kids don't have fathers?

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.120
Children do worse in 70 different areas.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.600
They're far more likely to be disobedient,

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.000
delinquent, drop out of school.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.054
Fathers are critical, says Farrell

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.640
because men tend to parent differently.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:06.260
For example, men roughhouse more with kids.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.220
Why is that important?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.600
Roughhousing creates so many skill sets.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.960
The father's creating a bond with the child,

00:03:14.969 --> 00:03:16.664
so the children don't mind the discipline

00:03:16.664 --> 00:03:18.659
because the discipline is the price they pay

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.220
for more fun with dad.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.960
People think that mothers tend to be better parents

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.220
because on average,

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.420
they're more attentive to children's needs.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.940
Mothers are more empathetic as a rule to the children

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.880
than dads, but an empathetic

00:03:31.889 --> 00:03:34.434
parent does not create an empathetic child.

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.269
An empathetic parent is someone

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:38.620
who's always thinking of the children's needs,

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.650
which teach the children to always

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.600
have his or her needs thought of.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.030
The empathy is created by the father or the mother,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.000
requiring the child to think about the father's needs,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:48.780
the mother's needs,

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.137
their brother's needs.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.760
In fact, he says helping children too much is harmful.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.940
Dr. Phil covered that in this video clip.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.520
Moms are filled with love

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.240
and they want to make sure their children do well,

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.140
so they often do for the children.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.520
Dads are filled with love but the way

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.620
that dads love

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.520
is to feel that I need to love the children

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.780
by having the children

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.540
learn how to do for themselves.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.669
Having both an involved mother and father leads

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:40.462
to the best outcome for kids.

00:04:40.462 --> 00:04:42.750
A government summary of studies

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.844
notes children who live with their fathers

00:04:44.844 --> 00:04:46.889
are more likely to have good physical and

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:49.945
emotional health, to achieve academically,

00:04:49.945 --> 00:04:53.320
to avoid drugs, violence, and delinquent behavior.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.084
We need men to be involved in the fathering role

00:04:58.084 --> 00:04:59.660
to a much greater degree

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.689
than they are and have been.

00:05:01.689 --> 00:05:04.919
Even when we control for the amount of money

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:06.540
a father and mother earn,

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.600
children with dads still do much better.

